/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:1:# Statuses
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:11:| **to-review** | Code ready for review | sub-agent |
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:12:| **reviewing** | Reviewer child is checking the work | reviewer |
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:13:| **integrating** | Accepted Change Request, not landed. Active, never terminal | `accept_cr` only; left only by the integration transaction |
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:14:| **done** | Reviewed and accepted leaf work, or computed container completion | integration transaction for Change Request work; reviewer verdict plus the acknowledged transition for inline work; parent aggregation |
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:18:## Status Flow
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:22:backlog → analysis → to-dev → development → to-review → reviewing → integrating → done
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:26:delta produced in a managed Story workspace. `accept_cr` is the only way in and
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:29:`reviewing → done` on the reviewer's accepted verdict, with the commit
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:32:**Returns from reviewing:**
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:33:- `reviewing → analysis` — need more research
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:34:- `reviewing → to-dev` — code issues, needs rework
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:41:**Note on closed:** Use `closed` for cancelled, obsolete, or won't-do items. Don't delete — close with a note explaining why. History is preserved. `handoff` refuses terminal elements; `set_status` refuses leaving `done` or `closed` with `TerminalStatusError` (`terminal_status`), naming the current terminal state. An identical `set_status` is idempotent.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:65:**Orchestrator review routing flow:** When a producer child sets `to-review`:
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:67:2. Orchestrator spawns a reviewer child with explicit selection, for example `task-board spawn TASK-... --role reviewer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max`.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:68:3. Reviewer child sets/keeps `reviewing`, reads artifacts/code, and writes the verdict.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:70:4a. When the reviewer was launched against a Change Request (a managed Story workspace run), acceptance is recorded by `accept_cr(ID, revision=N, evidence=...)` instead. That mutation writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically: it sets the Change Request to `accepted`, stamps the reviewer run, binds the revision to its **producer role and archetype**, and routes the element to `integrating` — accepted but not landed, and accepted work never stays in `reviewing`. The Orchestrator routes a new tracked run carrying that exact producer role and archetype; that run — not the Orchestrator — runs `task-board worktree checkpoint <ID>` for a **non-final** leaf, which commits the accepted candidate onto the Story branch and leaves the leaf `integrating`. A Change Request with `repository_delta=empty` creates no commit and likewise stays `integrating`. `done` is produced only by the integration transaction, and `worktree checkpoint` or `worktree integrate` from a reviewer, an orchestrator, or any run whose role/archetype is not the bound producer's is refused. `accept_cr` accepts no `commit_ack` argument, its `evidence` must be a task-scoped outcome resource this reviewer run attached or updated (naming the producer's own `_results.md` is refused with `change_request_evidence_missing`), only the reviewer run that was handed the revision may call it (anything else is refused with `change_request_acceptance_unauthorized`), and the live task/reviewer checklist must be complete. All refusals precede CR, status, and activity writes.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:75:5. On changes requested, the Orchestrator preserves the verdict, spawns the appropriate producer, and sends the next `to-review` handoff through a new reviewer. Repeat producer -> reviewer -> rework -> reviewer until accepted `done`.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:76:6. If a child exits early or leaves the item parked in `analysis`, `development`, `testing`, or `reviewing`, the Orchestrator inspects the run/outcomes and retries or reroutes through a focused child. Recoverable work is never handed to the human.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:79:`reviewing` is a real state, not a pass-through. A reviewer child must do actual review work between the producer handoff and `done`; the orchestrator routes and monitors that review instead of performing the verdict inline.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:81:`reviewing` is never a verdict, including under the Change Request flow. A reviewer run that ends at `reviewing` with no accepted Change Request is cancelled and a successor reviewer is spawned — that is what distinguishes "the reviewer decided nothing" from "the reviewer decided", and `accept_cr` does not change it. The accepted branch is derived from the Change Request record, not from the `reviewing` status.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:83:`to-review` therefore means one thing: a producer handoff awaiting review. An accepted Change Request is `integrating`, never `to-review`; `task-board worktree status` and the Change Request state say how far that integration has come.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:85:A tracked spawned producer cannot use direct `set_status(..., status=to-review)`
